    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/1311.4905v3</id>
    <title>The covariance of almost-primes in $\mathbb{F}_q[T]$</title>
    <updated>2014-08-09T03:09:07Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1311.4905v3" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/1311.4905v3" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>We estimate the covariance in counts of almost-primes in $\mathbb{F}_q[T]$, weighted by higher-order von Mangoldt functions. The answer takes a pleasant algebraic form. This generalizes recent work of Keating and Rudnick that estimates the variance of primes, and makes use, as theirs, of a recent equidistribution result of Katz.
  In an appendix we prove some related identities for random matrix statistics, which allows us to give a quick proof of a $2\times2$ ratio theorem for the characteristic polynomial of the unitary group. We additionally identify arithmetic functions whose statistics mimic those of hook Schur functions.</summary>
    <category term="math.NT" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <category term="math-ph" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
